"Rune: Marking": {
  "index": 0,
  "category": "runesmithing",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Rune: Marking"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "The "
        },
        {
          "text": "Rune of Marking",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " is used to mark a location, and is used to target certain rituals and spells. \n\n"
        },
        {
          "text": "Using the rune on a given block will store the block's coordinates and direction within the rune.",
          "italic": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "When holding a rune that has a position set on it in my main hand, I will see a green marker at the position. If the rune is held in my offhand, I will see a red marker. \n\nIf I hold two runes, one in each hand with a position set, you will also see a yellow zone indicating which area the two runes mark out."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Runes of marking can be dyed.  The dyed color can be cleared by washing the rune in a cauldron of water."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "A rune of marking can be placed into a crafting grid to clear its marked position, allowing it to stack again.  Clearing the marked position in this way will not clear the dye color (although the crafting grid preview will not show this)."
    }
  ],
  "related_recipes": [
